## Dependency Rules
- **Before adding any npm package**: check if Astro or browser already provides it
- **No React** — use Astro components + vanilla JS for interactivity
- **Exception**: small, focused libraries for games are OK (e.g., canvas helpers)
- Run `npm ls` to check actual installed packages before adding duplicates
- Prefer packages with zero dependencies themselves
- Check package size with `bundlephobia.com` before adding

## Code Style Rules
- All files: TypeScript (`.ts`, `.astro`)
- No `any` type — use `unknown` and narrow, or generate Supabase types
- No `console.log` in production — use conditional `import.meta.env.DEV`
- Mobile-first CSS — write for 320px, use `md:` and `lg:` prefixes to scale up
- Accessible HTML: `alt` on all images, ARIA labels on interactive elements
- Semantic HTML: `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<section>`, `<aside>`

## SEO Rules (Every Page)
- One `<h1>` per page
- Unique `<title>` and `<meta name="description">` per page
- `<meta property="og:*">` for social sharing
- `<link rel="canonical">` on every page
- Sitemap generated by `@astrojs/sitemap`
